# ── Not for a public repository ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A public GitHub repo publishes these at a stable, indexable URL. That is the
# same act as putting them on the site, and each one is something the site
# deliberately does not say:
#
#   portfolio-requirements_1.md   Names the DCS vendor evaluation, the module
#                                 count, the department's internal workflows and
#                                 an in-progress platform decision — the exact
#                                 material BLOCKING-1 says to keep off the public
#                                 web. The document arguing for the discretion
#                                 would itself be the disclosure.
#
#   bracu_alter.jpg               BRACU Alter team promotional card carrying
#   BracuAlter.jfif               head-and-shoulders photographs of nine named
#                                 people; and a TV news graphic under a
#                                 broadcaster's copyright. Neither is Niaz's to
#                                 republish, which is why neither is on the site
#                                 (BLOCKING-4).
#
#   Niaz Nafi Rahman_CV.pdf       The unredacted CV: his phone number, and two
#                                 referees' names, work emails and a mobile
#                                 number. §3 forbids publishing these. The
#                                 redacted copy that ships lives at
#                                 client/public/cv.pdf.
#
# They stay on disk; they just do not travel. Keep the requirements document —
# it is the reference for every decision here — just not in public.
portfolio-requirements_1.md
bracu_alter.jpg
BracuAlter.jfif
Niaz Nafi Rahman_CV.pdf
dp.jpg

# ── Generated, and safe to regenerate from a clean clone ───────────────────
# Both are derived from content/source.mjs, which is committed. `npm run build`
# regenerates them before bundling, so a fresh clone needs nothing else.
client/src/data/content.json
supabase/migrations/0002_portfolio_seed.sql

# ── Committed on purpose: the media the site is made of ────────────────────
#
# client/public/{artwork,fonts,photo}, og.png, cv.pdf
# client/src/styles/fonts.css
# client/src/data/artwork-manifest.json
#
# These are *derived* files, so the instinct is to ignore them. They are
# committed anyway, and the reason is worth stating: their inputs live outside
# this repository.
#
#   the ambigram renditions   come from the ghurnilipi project's build workspace,
#                             which gitignores them because the bytes live in its
#                             Supabase Storage bucket
#   the woff2 subsets         come from that project's next/font download cache
#   the measured rotation     takes ~4s of image analysis to reproduce
#   centres and font CSS      and is derived from those same files
#
# So a clone that did not carry them could not build, and would depend on a
# sibling checkout and a Supabase bucket to become buildable again. Committing
# them is what makes this repository self-contained and the built site
# same-origin: no CDN, no raw.githubusercontent, no third-party host on the LCP
# path for a visitor on Bangladeshi mobile data.
#
# `npm run assets` re-imports them when the sources are available, and skips
# quietly when they are not.
